## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where the Control UI's `tasks.list` poll stalls the gateway event loop on busy installs. Each call cloned and O(n log n) sorted every task record by `createdAt`, then immediately re-sorted the filtered set by last activity and sliced a bounded page — so the `createdAt` sort was thrown away, and the full re-sort ran across the entire registry on every poll. On gateways with thousands of accumulated completed/failed tasks this produced a noticeable event-loop stall per RPC (#101716).

Closes #101716.

## Why This Change Was Made

Two changes remove the wasted work while keeping the wire output byte-for-byte identical:

1. **Skip the discarded `createdAt` sort.** A new `listTaskRecordsUnsorted()` returns cloned records without the registry's newest-created sort (and the `insertionIndex` bookkeeping that only exists to support it). The `tasks.list` handler re-sorts by last activity anyway, so the registry sort was pure waste.
2. **Only sort the window the client needs.** `partialSortTopK` quickselects the `cursor + limit` window and fully sorts just that window — O(n + k log k) instead of O(n log n) — with a full-sort fallback when `k >= n`.

The page comparator (`taskUpdatedAt` desc, `taskId` asc) is unchanged, and since `taskId` is unique the order is a total order, so quickselect's non-stability cannot change results.

## User Impact

Operators of busy gateways get snappier Control UI task-list polling and no per-poll event-loop stalls as the task registry grows over days of uptime. Paging behavior and ordering are unchanged.

## Evidence

- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway-methods.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/tasks.test.ts` → **9 passed** (re-verified after merging latest `main`).
- New pagination test (pages past the first page) and a new equivalence test that pages through 12 records with mixed distinct/duplicate `lastEventAt` values and asserts the collected order across all pages exactly matches a full-sort reference — exercising both the partial-sort (`k < n`) path and the full-sort (`k >= n`) path, plus the `taskId` tie-break. Repeated 6× to confirm the randomized quickselect pivot is not flaky.
- `oxlint` clean; `tsgo:test:src` (test typecheck) clean.

### Large-registry benchmark (real behavior proof)

Standalone Node 24 (`tsx`) benchmark over a **10,000-record** synthetic registry — mixed statuses, spread `lastEventAt` with ties — exercising the exact `tasks.list` selection step on identical data for both code paths. **OLD** = verbatim `main` body (`listTaskRecords()` + full `.toSorted()`); **NEW** = this PR (`listTaskRecordsUnsorted()` + `partialSortTopK`). 25 runs each (8 warmup discarded), median; registry setup excluded. No status/agent/session filter (the worst case where every record reaches the sort).

**(A) Full page selection step:**

| Poll (limit 100) | OLD (main) | NEW (this PR) | Speedup |
|---|---|---|---|
| First page, cursor=0 (Control UI hot path) | 96.2 ms | 1.5 ms | **65.7×** |
| Deep page, cursor=9900 (k=n → partial sort falls back to full sort) | 94.8 ms | 4.3 ms | **21.9×** |

**(B) Isolated registry snapshot — what optimization #1 removes:**

| Snapshot call | Median |
|---|---|
| `listTaskRecords()` (clone + `createdAt` sort + `insertionIndex` bookkeeping) | 94.9 ms |
| `listTaskRecordsUnsorted()` (clone only) | 0.74 ms |

The discarded `createdAt` sort and its supporting per-record bookkeeping (`Object.assign` + `insertionIndex` add/strip — ~3 object allocations per record vs. 1) dominate `main`'s per-poll cost under GC pressure; that ~95 ms is what this PR removes on every poll. The `byUpdated` sort itself is cheap (~3.6 ms for 10k), which is why the deep-page win (where `partialSortTopK` still does a full sort) comes almost entirely from optimization #1.

**(C) Within NEW — optimization #2 (partial sort vs full sort):** first page (k=100) **1.5 ms** vs deep page (k=10000) **4.3 ms** — quickselect bounds the sort to the 100-element window on the hot path.

Absolute timings vary by machine/GC; the ratio is the stable signal. Representative single run; reproduction script below.

<details>
<summary>Benchmark script (drop at repo root, run <code>BENCH_N=10000 pnpm exec tsx bench-tasks-list.mts</code>)</summary>

```ts
// bench-tasks-list.mts — decomposes the tasks.list win for PR #102202.
// (A) full page A/B OLD vs NEW, (B) isolated snapshot cost, (C) partial vs full sort.
import { performance } from "node:perf_hooks";
import fs from "node:fs/promises";
import os from "node:os";
import path from "node:path";
import {
  createTaskRecord as createTaskRecordOrNull,
  listTaskRecords,
  listTaskRecordsUnsorted,
  resetTaskRegistryForTests,
} from "./src/tasks/runtime-internal.js";
import type { TaskRecord } from "./src/tasks/task-registry.types.js";
import { mapTaskSummary, taskUpdatedAt } from "./src/gateway/server-methods/task-summary.js";

const N = Number(process.env.BENCH_N ?? 10_000);
const RUNS = 25;
const WARMUP = 8;
const log = (msg: string) => process.stderr.write(`${msg}\n`);

const byUpdated = (left: TaskRecord, right: TaskRecord): number => {
  const updatedDiff = taskUpdatedAt(right) - taskUpdatedAt(left);
  if (updatedDiff !== 0) return updatedDiff;
  return left.taskId < right.taskId ? -1 : left.taskId > right.taskId ? 1 : 0;
};

// partialSortTopK + helpers, verbatim from src/gateway/server-methods/tasks.ts
function partition<T>(arr: T[], left: number, right: number, compare: (a: T, b: T) => number): number {
  const pivotIdx = left + Math.floor(Math.random() * (right - left + 1));
  [arr[pivotIdx], arr[right]] = [arr[right], arr[pivotIdx]];
  const pivotVal = arr[right];
  let storeIdx = left;
  for (let i = left; i < right; i++) {
    if (compare(arr[i], pivotVal) < 0) { [arr[i], arr[storeIdx]] = [arr[storeIdx], arr[i]]; storeIdx++; }
  }
  [arr[storeIdx], arr[right]] = [arr[right], arr[storeIdx]];
  return storeIdx;
}
function quickselect<T>(arr: T[], k: number, compare: (a: T, b: T) => number): void {
  let left = 0; let right = arr.length - 1;
  while (left < right) {
    const pivot = partition(arr, left, right, compare);
    if (pivot === k) break;
    if (pivot < k) left = pivot + 1; else right = pivot - 1;
  }
}
function partialSortTopK<T>(arr: T[], k: number, compare: (a: T, b: T) => number): T[] {
  if (k <= 0) return arr;
  if (k >= arr.length) return arr.toSorted(compare);
  quickselect(arr, k - 1, compare);
  return arr.slice(0, k).toSorted(compare);
}

function newPathPage(cursor: number, limit: number) {
  const filtered = listTaskRecordsUnsorted();
  partialSortTopK(filtered, cursor + limit, byUpdated).slice(cursor, cursor + limit).map(mapTaskSummary);
}
function oldPathPage(cursor: number, limit: number) {
  listTaskRecords().toSorted(byUpdated).slice(cursor, cursor + limit).map(mapTaskSummary);
}

function median(values: number[]): number {
  const sorted = [...values].sort((a, b) => a - b);
  const mid = Math.floor(sorted.length / 2);
  return sorted.length % 2 ? sorted[mid] : (sorted[mid - 1] + sorted[mid]) / 2;
}
function bench(label: string, fn: () => void): number {
  for (let i = 0; i < WARMUP; i++) fn();
  const samples: number[] = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < RUNS; i++) { const start = performance.now(); fn(); samples.push(performance.now() - start); }
  const med = median(samples);
  console.log(`  ${label.padEnd(42)} median=${med.toFixed(3)}ms`);
  return med;
}

async function main() {
  const stateDir = await fs.mkdtemp(path.join(os.tmpdir(), "openclaw-bench-tasks-"));
  process.env.OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR = stateDir;
  resetTaskRegistryForTests();
  const statuses = ["succeeded", "failed", "running", "cancelled", "timed_out"] as const;
  const t0 = performance.now();
  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
    createTaskRecordOrNull({
      runtime: "cli", requesterSessionKey: "agent:main:main", ownerKey: "agent:main:main",
      scopeKind: "session", runId: `run-bench-${i}`, task: `Bench task ${i}`,
      status: statuses[i % statuses.length], deliveryStatus: "not_applicable",
      lastEventAt: (i * 2654435761) % 9_000_000,
    });
  }
  log(`[bench] registry ready: ${N} records, setup ${(performance.now() - t0).toFixed(0)}ms (excluded)`);
  console.log(`\ntasks.list benchmark — ${N} records, ${RUNS} runs (median, ${WARMUP} warmup discarded)`);
  console.log("(A) Full page selection step — OLD (main) vs NEW (this PR):");
  const oldFirst = bench("OLD first page  cursor=0 limit=100", () => oldPathPage(0, 100));
  const newFirst = bench("NEW first page  cursor=0 limit=100", () => newPathPage(0, 100));
  const oldDeep = bench(`OLD deep page  cursor=${N - 100} limit=100`, () => oldPathPage(N - 100, 100));
  const newDeep = bench(`NEW deep page  cursor=${N - 100} limit=100`, () => newPathPage(N - 100, 100));
  console.log(`  -> first page: ${(oldFirst / newFirst).toFixed(1)}x; deep page: ${(oldDeep / newDeep).toFixed(1)}x`);
  console.log("\n(B) Isolated registry snapshot cost — what optimization #1 removes:");
  const oldSnap = bench("listTaskRecords()  (clone + createdAt sort + bookkeep)", () => { listTaskRecords(); });
  const newSnap = bench("listTaskRecordsUnsorted()  (clone only)", () => { listTaskRecordsUnsorted(); });
  console.log(`  -> snapshot: ${(oldSnap / newSnap).toFixed(1)}x cheaper`);
  console.log("\n(C) Within NEW — optimization #2 (partial sort vs full sort):");
  console.log(`  -> partial sort (k=100): ${newFirst.toFixed(3)}ms  vs  full sort (k=${N}): ${newDeep.toFixed(3)}ms`);
  resetTaskRegistryForTests({ persist: false });
  await fs.rm(stateDir, { recursive: true, force: true });
}
main().catch((error) => { process.stderr.write(`[bench] ERROR: ${String(error?.stack ?? error)}\n`); process.exit(1); });
```

</details>

## Notes

This combines and completes two earlier partial attempts (both still open with failing checks):
- #102132 added `listTaskRecordsUnsorted()` but left the full handler re-sort in place (`check-test-types` failed).
- #102118 added `partialSortTopK` but still called the sorted `listTaskRecords()` (`check-lint` failed).

This PR takes both ideas, resolves both CI failures, and adds the equivalence regression neither had. Happy to rework or fold into one of those if a maintainer prefers.

Branch merged with latest `main` (was out-of-date).

